    "description": "BillingService, ShipmentRepository, TenantCache, and AuditLog currently represent customer, order, shipment, tenant, and session identifiers as plain strings, even though all are generated as UUIDs. Public methods such as findOrder(String), attachShipment(String, String), and routeByTenant(String, String) therefore accept interchangeable arguments. A recent release routed a shipment through a customer lookup and the incorrect record was retrieved without a runtime conversion error. The raw UUID must remain available only at infrastructure boundaries, while domain APIs should reject swapping identifier families before code runs. Every repository must still be able to persist and query its existing UUID column without separate lookup tables, and equality, serialization, and logging must remain predictable. The key decision is whether these semantically different identifiers receive separate static identities despite sharing the same underlying representation.",
    "decision_statement": "Should customer, order, shipment, tenant, and session identifiers be made statically distinct so their UUID representations cannot be accidentally interchanged?",
    "notes": "newtype primary: identifier families sharing a UUID representation must be statically distinct at domain APIs; value-object is the representation near-miss; immutable-object supports."
  },
